{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Raise the basic rate tax free allowance in line with the state pension for all",
        "additional_details": "The standard personal allowance is currently \u00a312,570.  From April 2027 the state pension will increase to \u00a313,036.  Pensioners whose only income is from the state pension will not pay any income tax.  We believe this discriminates against working people and pensioners who earn \u00a313,036 or more from employment or other pension income.  It should be the same threshold for everyone: as it rises from \u00a313,036 and upwards each year, as the state pension rises so the tax threshold should rise annually.",
        "background": "When the state pension rises above the basic rate tax allowance the Government proposes to fully exempt from tax only pensioners whose sole income is the state pension. We feel this discriminates against other people - the basic rate tax allowance should rise for everyone as the state pension rises.",
